0409.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scheppers</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>van Dongen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Dekker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Geertzen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dekker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Potential barriers to the use of health services among ethnic minorities: a review</article-title><source>Fam Prac</source><year>2006</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>348</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/fampra/cmi113</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Foundation</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><source>Using interpreters to access services: user views</source><series>Findings</series><year>2004</year><edition>September</edition><publisher-name>London, Joseph Rowntree Foundation</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Junod Perron</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hudelson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Somatisation: illness perspectives of asylum seekers and refugee patients from the former country of Yugoslavia</article-title><source>BMC Family Practice</source><year>2006</year><volume>7</volume><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16480514</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>